      "body": "## Motivation\nQSA chunk prefill reconstructs sequence-length metadata and synchronizes the device to infer a query-length bound already available to the caller.\n\n## Modifications\n- Reuse the batch sequence-length tensor.\n- Accept an optional known maximum query length, retaining the inferred-bound fallback for existing callers.\n- Add CUDA graph replay coverage with changed query inputs.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\nOn this commit, based on main at `f050ab194a`: the complete QSA test file passed with **51 passed, 1 skipped** on B200. Repository-configured Ruff checks and formatting passed.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\nNo isolated end-to-end speedup is claimed for this PR. Performance measurements for the complete series are reported in the companion KV packing PR; they were collected before rebasing to the current main.\n\n## Related PRs and merge order\nThis is a stacked series; each PR contains only its own incremental diff:\n1. #41932: prefill length metadata (base: main).\n2. #41933: fused KV gathering/conversion (base: #41932).\n3. #41934: compact grid for ragged batches (base: #41933).\n\nMerge in that order and retarget dependents as their bases land. The packing and compact-grid changes should land together to cover highly ragged workloads. The end-to-end numbers in #41933 describe the complete series, not three independent gains.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #36783054230](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/36783054230)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #36783053918](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/36783053918)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #36783054206](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/36783054206)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
